course: dictionary
lesson: 6292
title: Words that paint a picture
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words build a whole picture in one go. Moonlit is one of them. «Imagine a beach at night: tiny turtles pop out of the sand and race towards the brightest thing they can see, which is normally the moonlit sea.» Moonlit is made of two parts, moon and lit. The moon lights it, so moonlit means lit by the light of the Moon.
explain: Look at what the words around moonlit tell you. The sea is at night, and the turtles race towards it because it is the brightest thing they can see. So the sea is shining, but not with lamps or the Sun. It is glowing softly under the Moon.
explain: Writers choose moonlit when they want a calm, quiet or magical scene. A moonlit garden or a moonlit road sounds peaceful, and sometimes a little spooky. You feel this from the picture, not just the dictionary meaning.
explain: Now read the second sentence: «Bright beach lights confuse turtle hatchlings, which crawl towards the lights instead of the moonlit sea.» The bright lights are a problem because they pull the baby turtles the wrong way. The moonlit sea is the right way to go. Context shows you why a word matters.
fact: Moonlit means lit by the light of the Moon.
fact: The word is built from moon and lit, so you can work it out from its parts.
fact: «The moonlit sea» is a place lit softly by the Moon, not by the Sun or street lamps.
fact: Writers use moonlit in stories and poems to create calm, magical or spooky feelings.
fact: In «Bright beach lights confuse turtle hatchlings», the bright lights are bad for the baby turtles because they lead them away from the moonlit sea.
exercise: «The moonlit sea sparkled under the silver sky.» What does moonlit mean? | Covered in sand | Full of waves | *Lit by the light of the Moon | Very cold
exercise: «Bright beach lights confuse turtle hatchlings, which crawl towards the lights instead of the moonlit sea.» Why do the hatchlings go the wrong way? | They want to find their mothers on the sand | They are tired and want to sleep | *The bright lights pull them away from the sea | They are chasing crabs
exercise: Which word in «the moonlit sea» is built from two smaller words, moon and lit? | Pick the word that contains the word moon. | sea | the | *moonlit | sea
test: What does moonlit mean? | Very windy and wet | Frozen solid | *Lit by the light of the Moon | Dark and cloudy
test: A writer describes «a moonlit garden». What feeling does this most likely give? | Bright as midday | Loud and busy | *Calm and magical | Hot and crowded
exam: Which sentence uses moonlit correctly? | The sun was moonlit at noon. | *The moonlit sea shone silver under the night sky. | The moonlit children ran to school at breakfast. | My moonlit lunch was very hot.
